# Keep the build context to source only. Everything below is either
# regenerable, local-only, or irrelevant to `go build`, and shipping it would
# slow the build and widen the set of bytes the daemon has to look at.
.git
.github
.agent-artifacts
docs
deploy
# The only directories the image copies from the repository are cmd/,
# internal/ and sql/. Docker's ignore rules are last-match-wins, so anything
# that had to stay in the context would need its parents re-included first.
#
# `fixtures` is ignored as a whole: the hand-authored Riot payloads under it are
# the tests' input, not the image's, and the demo tree at fixtures/site was only
# ever copied for the retired web tier.
fixtures
# The checked-in Data Dragon projection is a designer's and a test's input, not
# the image's. The upstream-shaped payloads the crawler tests read are a
# different tree, at fixtures/ddragon/, and are excluded with the rest of
# fixtures/.
projection
# The generated artifact shape cmd/gen-types writes. internal/aggmodel owns the
# document and the image emits it from there, so the copy on disk is a
# reviewer's and a test's input rather than the image's.
schema
*.md
bin
node_modules

# Secrets never enter a build context, even though nothing here copies them.
.env
*.pem
*.key
